// Delays in equations. a -> b is a in the first tick and b afterwards. a fby b is a in the first tick and the
// previous tick's b afterwards (a -> pre(b) is rewritten to a fby b). pre(x) is the previous tick's x, and 0
// (false for bool) in the first tick whatever the declared initial value.
scchart St42Delays {
  input int I = 7
  output int arrow, followed, arrowPre, previous
  dataflow {
    arrow = 0 -> I
    followed = 0 fby I
    arrowPre = 0 -> pre(I)
    previous = pre(I)
  }
}
